// # core/mem — Linear Arena + ARC + Alignment
//
// Logline: The O(1) bulk-reset linear arena, the deterministic ARC (atomic ref-counted), and the 64-byte aligned payload allocator (OO_PAYLOAD_ALIGN = 64). v2.0.0: all weak-ref and control-block mutators require AllocCap.
//
// Beats:
//   1. weak.h — OoControlBlock + OoWeakRef + OO_FLAG_* values.
//   2. weak.c — the C11-atomic retain/release semantics (v2.0.0: cap-gated).
//   3. arena.c — orchestrator: linear arena create/alloc/reset/destroy + the 32-slot g_ar[] table.
//   4. arena_pin.c — CPU pinning for stable arena/dudect timing (sched_setaffinity / pthread_setaffinity_np).
//   5. arena_soa.c — SoA (Structure-of-Arrays) layout calculation.
//   6. arena_dod.c — DoD (Data-oriented Design) layout calculation.
//   7. arena_checkpoint.c — checkpoint/rollback + Welch double-run determinism proof.
//   8. alloc.c — bulk allocator that backs the arena (v2.0.0: oo_alloc/free/write_int/read_int cap-gated).
//   9. align.c — 64-byte aligned payload primitive.
//
// v2.3.0 file split: the original 394-line arena.c was split into
// arena.c (orchestrator) + arena_pin.c + arena_soa.c + arena_dod.c +
// arena_checkpoint.c. The split is functional (one concept per file):
// pinning, SoA, DoD, and checkpoint are independent concerns.
//
// ──▓▓ core/mem ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: Pillar 7 — deterministic, no GC ::
